        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new `OwnerSegment` class is otherwise exemplary: it mirrors the established derivation-helper idiom in this package exactly (`final` class, private constructor, static `of(Owner)`, named constants, thorough javadoc cross-linking the DTO field) \u2014 structurally indistinguishable from `AgeBand` and `ContactPreference`, and placing it in `mapper` beside its siblings and wiring it through a `@Mapping` expression is the natural fit. One concrete finding:\n\n**Duplicated \"known regions\" set \u2014 region knowledge is deliberately centralized elsewhere.**\n`OwnerSegment` hardcodes its own `KNOWN_REGIONS = Set.of(\"NSW\", \"VIC\", \"QLD\")`. But the set of known regions is already authoritatively enumerated in `Regions.java` \u2014 it's the key set of `REGION_POSTCODES` / `REGION_TIMEZONE` and the value set of `CITY_REGION`. This codebase goes to unusual lengths to keep region facts in one place (see `Regions.UNKNOWN` pointing at `CustomerCode.UNKNOWN_REGION` with javadoc explicitly stating the two \"can never diverge\", and `CustomerCode.format`/`region` documented as a matched pair). Re-listing `{NSW, VIC, QLD}` in a third, independent spot breaks that pattern: adding a fourth region later means updating `Regions`' three maps *and* remembering this set, and a maintainer would reasonably expect \"is this a known region?\" to be answered by `Regions`, not re-derived in the mapper helper.\n\nSuggested fix: expose the membership test from `Regions` (the owner of region knowledge) \u2014 e.g. a `Regions.isKnownRegion(String)` predicate backed by the existing maps \u2014 and have `OwnerSegment.of` call it, so the known-region list stays single-sourced. `OwnerSegment` keeps the `PREMIUM_FROM` tier constant and the formatting logic, which are genuinely its own concern."
